  "notice": "Hand-built retrieval eval set (PROJECT_PLAN.md §10). Relevance is judged at logical_provision_id level and resolved to the versioned_provision_id valid on relevant_date in the corpus being evaluated, so the metrics are scored at version level (SYSTEM_SPEC.md §18). 'terminology' queries use precise legal references (article numbers, Annex III points and area names), where BM25 is expected to matter most. 'use_case' queries describe a situation in plain language with no article numbers. 'temporal' queries run against the synthetic multi-version fixture; they are phrased in the amended wording, so on a pre-amendment date the newer, ineligible version is the closer lexical and semantic match. POST-HOC ADDITION (2026-10-02): the 'terminology_bare' and 'terminology_variant' queries (ids B*, V*) were added AFTER the first evaluation run, because the original 'terminology' queries carry topical words and saturated every arm at Recall@5 = 1.0. They are not a pre-planned benchmark. B01-B10 ('seen_in_probe': true) were also used in an informal probe before being added, so their results were known in advance; B11-B26 and V01-V07 were written without being run. 'terminology_variant' uses citation styles the BM25 tokenizer was not written for ('Art. 26(6)', 'Annex III, point 4(a)', 'point (h) of Article 5(1)'), and the tokenizer was deliberately not changed to fit them. The original 65-query run is frozen in data/eval/results/baseline_v1_65q*.",
